{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
  "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Robert Mallory worked for Norfolk Southern as a freight-car mechanic for nearly 20 years, frst in Ohio, then in Virginia."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Pennsylvania Supreme Court sided with Norfolk Southern."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Norfolk Southern",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Norfolk Southern argues that the Due Process Clause entitles it to a more favorable rule, one shielding it from suits even its employees must answer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mallory",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0000-0006",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He also demolished car interiors that, he alleges, contained carcinogens."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mallory",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "By complying with this statutory scheme, Mr. Mallory contended, Norfolk Southern had consented to suit in Pennsylvania on claims just like his."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0001-0001",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the law had long permitted suits against individuals in any jurisdiction where they could be found, no matter where the underlying cause of action happened to arise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Norfolk Southern",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Norfolk Southern suggests that this Court's decision in International Shoe Co. v. Washington, 326 U. S. 310 (1945), has already done much of the hard work for us. That decision, the company insists, seriously undermined Pennsylvania Fire's foundations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0002-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Contrary to what it says in its brief here, the company even proclaimed itself a proud part of \u201cthe Pennsylvania Community.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Public Citizen",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Brief for Public Citizen as Amicus Curiae 21."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Norfolk Southern",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It argues that it has not really submitted to proceedings in Pennsylvania."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Norfolk Southern",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Brief for Respondent 16\u201319; see post, at 168\u2013171 (opinion of Barrett, J.)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0002-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because that decision remains the law, the judgment of the Supreme Court of Pennsylvania is vacated, and the case is remanded."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0002-0007",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I agree with the Court that this case is straightforward under our precedents. I write separately to say that, for me, what makes it so is not just our ruling in Pennsylvania Fire Ins. Co. of Philadelphia v. Gold Issue Mining & Milling Co., 243 U. S. 93 (1917). I also consider our ruling in Insurance Corp. of Ireland v. Compagnie des Bauxites de Guinee, 456 U. S. 694 (1982), to be particularly instructive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Norfolk Southern",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Norfolk Southern's \u201cconduct and connection with [Pennsylvania] are such that [it] should reasonably anticipate being haled into court there.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Academy of Rail Labor Attorneys",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0003-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Brief for Academy of Rail Labor Attorneys as Amicus Curiae 4\u20135 (collecting cases);"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Tanya Monestier",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1168",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5149e9957088-0003-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
